===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[geographic]] area [[own]]ed or [[controlled]] by a single [[person]] or [[organization]].
#: {{ux|en|The king ruled his '''domain''' harshly.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1954|month=February|author=Trevor Holloway|title=Canada's Transcontinental Routes|journal=Railway Magazine|page=128|text=Bears and other ferocious beasts resented man's intrusion into their '''domain'''; so, too, did the Blackfoot Indians and other tribes, whose savage hostility was a constant menace to the lives of the toiling engineers.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=25 February 2020|url=https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2020/feb/25/the-end-of-farming-rewilding-intensive-agriculture-food-safety|author=Christopher de Bellaigue|title=The end of farming?|passage=Farmers account for just 1.5% of the British population, but the size of their '''domain''' – 71% of the country’s surface area is classified as farmland – has given them power over the public imagination.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist={{w|Nergal (musician)|Nergal}}, {{w|Tomasz Wróblewski}}|composer={{w|Behemoth (band)|Behemoth}}||title=Ov My Herculean Exile|album={{w|Opvs Contra Natvram}}|artist={{w|Behemoth (band)|Behemoth}}|year=2022|passage=A blinded hermit in oblivion, disgraced<br/>Like Odysseus lost in Poseidon's endless '''domain'''<br/>In a realm devoid ov solace, I roam}}
# A [[field]] or [[sphere of influence|sphere]] of [[activity]], [[influence]] or [[expertise]].
#: {{ux|en|Dealing with complaints isn't really my '''domain''': get in touch with customer services.}}
#: {{ux|en|His '''domain''' is English history.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Müjdat Erarkadaş; Kübra Özmeral Erarkadaş; Şahika Gülen Şişmanlar|title= Autism Spectrum Disorder Beyond Childhood: A Comprehensive Assessment of Activities of Daily Living and Social Functioning in Turkish Adults.|doi=10.1007/s10803-025-06969-8|date=2025-08-13|work=Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders|url=https://link-springer-com.wikipedialibrary.idm.oclc.org/article/10.1007/s10803-025-06969-8|passage=When examining studies that assess independent living and social skills—key areas of focus in adulthood for individuals with ASD—it is observed that most research evaluates only one of these '''domains''', either activities of daily living or social functioning.}}
# A [[group]] of [[related]] [[item]]s, [[topic]]s, or [[subject]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-01|author=Michael Riordan|title=Tackling Infinity|volume=100| issue=1| page=86| magazine=w:American Scientist|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/tackling-infinity| passage=Some of the most beautiful and thus appealing physical theories, including quantum electrodynamics and quantum gravity, have been dogged for decades by infinities that erupt when theorists try to prod their calculations into new '''domains'''. Getting rid of these nagging infinities has probably occupied far more effort than was spent in originating the theories.| accessdate=12 May 2013| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130430074403/http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/tackling-infinity| archivedate=30 April 2013}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|set theory}} The set of [[input]] ([[argument]]) values for which a [[function]] is defined.
## {{lb|en|more generally|of a [[binary relation]] R between A and B}} The set ''A''; The [[subset]] of ''A'' consisting of [[element]]s ''a'' of ''A'' such that there exists an element ''b'' in ''B'' with ''(a,b)'' in ''R''.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A {{l|en|ring}} with no [[zero divisor]]s; that is, in which no {{l|en|product}} of nonzero elements is zero.
#: {{hyponyms|en|integral domain}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|topology|analysis}} An open and connected set in some [[topology]]. For example, the interval (0,1) as a subset of the [[real number]]s.
# {{senseid|en|any DNS domain name}} {{lb|en|computing|Internet}} Any [[Domain Name System|DNS]] [[domain name]], particularly one which has been [[delegate|delegated]] and has become representative of the delegated domain name and its [[subdomain]]s.
#* '''2000''', ''BIND 9 Administrator Reference Manual (9.3.2)'', Internet Software Consortium [https://web.archive.org/web/20060619063455/http://www.bind9.net/manual/bind/9.3.2/Bv9ARM.ch01.html]
#*: Every name in the DNS tree is a '''domain''', even if it is terminal, that is, has no subdomains.
# {{lb|en|computing|Internet}} A collection of [[Domain Name System|DNS]] or DNS-like [[domain name|domain names]] consisting of a [[delegate|delegated]] [[domain name]] and all its [[subdomain]]s.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A collection of information having to do with a domain, the [[computer]]s named in the domain, and the [[network]] on which the computers named in the domain reside.
# {{lb|en|computing}} The collection of computers identified by a domain's [[domain name]]s.
# {{lb|en|physics}} A small region of a magnetic material with a consistent magnetization direction.
# {{lb|en|computing}} Such a region used as a data storage element in a [[bubble memory]].
# {{lb|en|data processing}} A form of technical [[metadata]] that represent the type of a data item, its characteristics, name, and usage.
#* {{quote-web|en|year=a. 2013|author=IBM|title=IBM Terminology - terms D| site='IBM Software{{!}}Globalization{{!}}Terminology'| url=https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/ecm/10.1.0?topic=objects-data-domains| accessdate=2013-12-29| passage=A characteristic of a field. A data domain specifies a data type and applies the minimum and maximum values allowed and other constraints.}}
# {{lb|en|taxonomy}} The highest [[rank]] in the classification of [[organism]]s, above [[kingdom]]; in the three-domain system, one of the [[taxon|taxa]] {{taxfmt|Bacteria|kingdom}}, {{taxfmt|Archaea|kingdom}}, or {{taxfmt|Eukaryota|superkingdom}}.
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} A [[folded]] section of a [[protein]] [[molecule]] that has a [[discrete]] [[function]]; the equivalent section of a [[chromosome]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} An area of more or less [[uniform]] [[mineralization]].

